-abort` is never escalated to `UNRECOVERABLE`, machine-managed [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]recovery never discards committed bead claims, and the recurring [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`sdd-sidecar` / `workspace_sdd_clone_recovery` axe error stops.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase/repos/plans/202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]sdd_clone_integration_race.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One critical section for bead mutation, commit, and [/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]integration[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]serialize[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'One critical section for bead mutation, commit, and integration' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: put the bead-store worktree materialization and its git commit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]inside the same store-write-lock critical section that SDD integration [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]already uses, so a claim's un-staged JSONL can never land inside another[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]process's rebase.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rollback verification asserts only SASE-owned invariants[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Rollback verification asserts only SASE-owned invariants' section: stop[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]treating a foreign worktree or untracked delta as proof that SASE broke [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the clone, so a clean `rebase --abort` reports the benign aborted status[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instead of escalating to `UNRECOVERABLE` and triggering destructive [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]recovery.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Conflict probes stop reporting git failures as \"no conflicts\"[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]probes[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Conflict probes stop reporting git failures as \"no conflicts\"' section:[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]make the unmerged-path and conflicted-file probes distinguish \"clean\" [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from \"could not tell\", route the bead conflict resolver's probes through[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the shared git-lock retry policy, and stop rewriting every event stream [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]on every conflict.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Machine-managed SDD git ignores the user's rerere config[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]rerere[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Machine-managed SDD git ignores the user's rerere config' section: [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]disable rerere for every SASE-issued git command in a machine-managed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SDD store and purge the resolution cache that the user's global [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`rerere.autoupdate` already leaked into the shared plans clone.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bound repeated doomed integration attempts[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]backoff[dim] · [dim][/dim]after verify[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Bound repeated doomed integration attempts' section: add a per-clone [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]failed-integration cooldown so a clone that cannot rebase is not [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]re-rebased about once per second, and report the suppressed attempts [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instead of hiding them.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Worktree-mutating callers wait for the store write lock [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]instead of failing open[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]lockwait[dim] · [dim][/dim]after serialize[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Worktree-mutating callers wait for the store write lock instead of [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]failing open' section: keep fail-open only where it is safe, and make [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the paths that mutate a shared SDD worktree either wait long enough [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]under contention or fail closed.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reconcile the discarded claims and reap the recovery residue[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]repair[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Reconcile the discarded claims and reap the recovery residue' section: [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]audit every retained recovery ref and stash in the shared plans clone [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]for bead state that never reached the remote, reconcile what is still [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]live, and add bounded reaping so the residue does not accumulate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]forever.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Concurrent-writer soak exercise[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]soak[dim] · [dim][/dim]after serialize, verify, probes, rerere, backoff, lockwait[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Concurrent-writer soak exercise' section: drive many concurrent bead [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]claims against one clone while integration runs and assert no [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`UNRECOVERABLE` outcome, no discarded local commit, and no axe error [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]digest entry.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-9r","hidden":false,"llm_provider":"codex","mode